{"name":"Zucchini Garden","hex":"#afa170","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"zucchini","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A courgette; a variety of squash, Cucurbita pepo, which bears edible fruit.","The edible fruit of this variety of squash."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["plural of zucchino"]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/zucchini"},{"term":"garden","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["An outdoor area containing one or more types of plants, usually plants grown for food or ornamental purposes.","Such an ornamental place to which the public have access."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To grow plants in a garden; to create or maintain a garden.","Of a batsman, to inspect and tap the pitch lightly with the bat so as to smooth out small rough patches and irregularities."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/garden"}],"entries":[{"title":"Zucchini","blocks":[{"text":"Zucchini, courgette, or Cucurbita pepo var. cylindrica is a summer squash, a vining herbaceous plant whose fruit are harvested when their immature seeds and epicarp (rind) are still soft and edible. It is closely related, but not identical, to the marrow; its fruit may be called marrow when mature."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/92/CSA-Striped-Zucchini.jpg/330px-CSA-Striped-Zucchini.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Zucchini","wikidata":"Q7533"},{"title":"Garden","blocks":[{"text":"A garden is a planned space, usually outdoors, set aside for the cultivation, display, and enjoyment of plants and other forms of nature. The single feature identifying even the wildest wild garden is control. The garden can incorporate both natural and artificial materials."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/41/Brooklyn_Botanic_Garden_New_York_May_2015_010.jpg/330px-Brooklyn_Botanic_Garden_New_York_May_2015_010